k_update={
 'K-ST01':'Actual D1 release and local reserve readiness on every vehicle, not head/tail pressure alone.32coach chambers plus actual locomotive branch count; prove mechanical release before propulsion permission.',
 'K-ST02':'Accept pressure-to-service-stroke-to-wheel-torque/load schedule with Type20service section and actual S-cam/slack geometry. Low-force modulation must suit empty/loaded rail adhesion in both directions; nominal diaphragm area is not brake torque.',
 'K-ST03':'With MR intact, BP emergency does not inherently vent spring-release chambers. Demonstrate every local service application, actual timing and stopped parking transfer without assuming spring application from BP loss.',
 'K-ST04':'Use D1 actual service and spring curves to prove holding transfer without excessive summed force or a restraint gap. Anti-compounding valve/control behavior must be accepted with the complete foundation brake.',
 'K-ST05':'BP-only leak/rupture with MR still charged can leave springs air-released. Prove leak/feed/vent discrimination and actual local service response, not just a full-separation demonstration.',
 'K-ST06':'MR-only loss requires local-reserve isolation and a proved command before usable reserve is lost. A check valve alone does not command braking; document subsequent spring-release depletion and actual force transition.',
 'K-ST07':'For each of4actual intervehicle joints, both portions need usable local braking and appropriate propulsion removal. Reconcile32coach chambers plus locomotive, cock/connector/isolation behavior and electrical-jumper persistence. No moving separation test authorized.',
 'K-ST08':'Record current brake DC versus hotel loss separately. Base pneumatic emergency cannot rely on software; actual spring default and service/spring overlap require measured torque/timing/slide evidence with accepted safe fixtures.',
 'K-ST09':'Use complete actual chambers/lines/reservoirs/valves and leakage/repeated-stop duty to establish usable reserve and compressor-loss response. Current compressor supply assignment and locomotive package remain unresolved.',
 'K-ST10':'Closed-cock/isolated-car faults can retain static pressure while losing command. Accepted continuity proof must observe commanded application AND release at every actual vehicle; no dispatch on pressure-only indication.',
 'K-ST11':'Prove detection of valid pilot but absent service pressure/mechanical torque in one D1 branch. Spring backup is not independent if the common cam/linkage/friction assembly is failed.',
 'K-ST12':'Retained service pressure or blocked exhaust can cause brake drag/heat/slide. Verify actual mechanical release and traction inhibit; do not add spring force blindly or accept an unapproved isolated-brake operating mode.',
 'K-ST13':'Actual reservoir/downstream hose fault must not silently deplete healthy reserves. Separate service/spring feeds and isolation need exact flow behavior; distinct schematic boxes do not demonstrate independence.',
 'K-ST14':'Distinguish release-hose rupture (local spring application) from blocked exhaust (parking may fail). D1 force asymmetry, trapped pressure, spring indication and anti-compounding need separate accepted evidence.',
 'K-ST15':'Mechanical release/caging removes normal spring holding. Use exact delivered OEM procedure only within independently restrained, separately authorized rescue; tag every disabled brake and restore/retest. No generic caging steps or passenger dispatch are authorized.',
 'K-ST16':'Requalify every-vehicle brake command/continuity and actual direction-dependent D1 behavior. R2 does not clear routine pushing/reversing/towing or occupied shunting; visibility and compressive couplings require separate accepted operating case.',
 'K-ST17':'Exact mechanically distinct BP/MR/control connectors, end termination, labels and isolation must be defined. Prove wrong/self-sealed/bridged-permit faults are detected; a label or network status alone is insufficient.',
 'K-ST18':'Shared S-cam/slack/shoe/drum/hub/carrier failure can defeat service AND spring parking even with normal pressure. Actual mechanical condition/stroke/output/drag and hub retention evidence must supplement air instrumentation.',
 'K-ST19':'Reconcile partial-cycle reserve depletion and actual every-vehicle recharge/release before traction permission.32coach catalog volume sum is not full-train readiness or recharge timing; parking release remains controlled.',
 'K-ST20':'Prove smallest credible BP leak and maximum actual charging/feed condition, not only open-pipe loss. Emergency vent/feed isolation and detection must overcome masking while MR may keep springs released.'}
